================================================================================
Vendored cores and the licence of a built image
================================================================================

The MIT terms above cover the first-party code in this repository: everything
under src/, include/, lib/gbcore/, lib/gnuboy_runner/, test/ and tools/.

The emulator core is vendored, and it decides the licence of a built image.

  lib/gnuboy/          gnuboy, as carried by retro-go, GPL-2.0-or-later. See
                       lib/gnuboy/COPYING for the full text and
                       lib/gnuboy/CREDITS for authorship. Every firmware image
                       links this core, so every image is a combined work with
                       GPL-2.0 code and is distributed under GPL-2.0-or-later.
                       The firmware handed to a user is therefore
                       GPL-2.0-or-later, and that user is entitled to the
                       corresponding source on request.

The MIT grant on the first-party code is unaffected: it stays MIT at the source
level, and the GPL obligation attaches only to the combined image
that links lib/gnuboy/.
